# P15 (docs/phase15-brief.md 6 item 8): a power-off with the codec in
# standby. The shell idles past the 5 s standby timer (the dac line shows
# standby=1), then the power button path runs (power_off_now: sys_poweroff()
# on this thread, the same SYS_POWEROFF broadcast), which on the device
# calls audiohw_close() from standby. The sim has no codec to hang, so
# this checks the shell's side: the power-off line is logged after the
# standby line, the run ends cleanly (shots.sh would time out otherwise)
# and no wake is counted by the power-off itself.
#   SIM_BUILD=build/sim-ui scripts/shots.sh tests/ui/ipodui-p15-standby-poweroff.script
# trace: p15dac
# dac: sleeps>=1
# logbetween: start idle dac standby=1 sleeps=1 wakes=0
# logafter: idle power off
# nolog: dac standby=0
# golden: skip idle

wait 7500
ab_mark idle
shot idle
power_off_now
wait 1000
quit
